// Network sync test scene, spawned by --server / --connect at a FIXED transform (main.cpp) so both
// sides hold identical entities: entities pair by explicit netIds. Gizmo-drag a render-only cube on
// the SERVER and the client copy follows at the snapshot rate; drag one on the CLIENT and it returns
// to the server's state on the next keyframe (nothing sends client -> server). The dynamic physics
// cubes (Ids 10+) drop onto the static ground and tumble: both sides simulate, the client corrects
// its bodies toward the server's poses/velocities and sleeps them when the server's sleep. Press K
// on either instance to fire the "NetPing" network event (logged on every connected instance).
Prefab networkTest
	Name "Network Test"
	Position 0 0 0
	Rotation 0 -0 0
	Scale 1
	Component Scene
		Entity NetCube1
			Position -6 0 0
			Scale 0.5
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer baseshapes
				Node Cube
				Type StaticMesh
			Component Network
				Id 1
